<td><h2>PNO: Technical discovery on Løvmeis prospect (PL1013)</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2024-11-26 14:05:19</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Reference is made to the stock notices on October 3rd. Drilling operations on the exploration well on the Løvmeis prospect in PL1013 have been concluded. The well is determined as a technical discovery and will be permanently plugged and abandoned. More details about the well results will be published by the Norwegian Offshore Directorate shortly.<br><br>PL1013 license partners: Equinor (Operator, 40%), ORLEN Upstream Norway AS (40%) and Petrolia Noco AS (20%).</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
<a target="_blank" href="https://petrolianoco.no/">
https://petrolianoco.no/</a>
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>PNO: Løvmeis (PL1013) commenced drilling</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2024-10-03 12:16:39</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Petrolia Noco AS (PNO) today announces that drilling has commenced on the Løvmeis Exploration Well 6608/10-R-2 H in the Norwegian Sea. The license was awarded in the APA 2018 with PNO as the initial operator. The operatorship has later been transferred to Equinor.<br><br>The Løvmeis well is being drilled by Transocean Encourage, a CAT D semi-submersible rig, owned and operated by Transocean. The well is being drilled from the Fossekall template at a water depth of 358 metres. <br><br>PL1013 licence partners: Equinor (Operator, 40%), PGNiG (40%), Petrolia Noco (20%) .</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
