<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>PNO: Awarded two licenses in APA 2023</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2024-01-16 23:19:11</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Bergen, 16 January 2024<br> <br>Petrolia Noco AS (PNO) is pleased to announce that it has been awarded interests in two licenses, including one operatorship under the Norwegian Awards in Predefined Areas (APA 2023) licensing round. <br> <br>License PL 1221 will be operated by PNO with a 40% working interest. License partner is Equinor with 60% working interest. The award will strengthen the company’s position in the Frøya High area in the Norwegian Sea where it already holds interest in PL 935. <br> <br>License PL 1210 will be operated by Wintershall DEA (40% working interest) with PNO and Equinor as license partners, both with 30% working interest. The license is located in the North Sea and is a potential play opening prospect.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
<a target="_blank" href="https://petrolianoco.no/">
https://petrolianoco.no/</a>
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>PNO: Acquisition of Brage completed</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2023-12-29 10:52:38</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Bergen, December 29th 2023 <br><br>Petrolia Noco AS is pleased to announce that the acquisition of 12.2575 percent interest in the Brage Field from Vår Energi ASA (OSE: VAR) that was announced on October 6th 2023, has been approved by the authorities with an effective date of January 1st 2023 and was completed today. <br><br> “We are pleased with the transaction and the new potential in the Brage Field and look forward to working with the license partners to uncover further value in the asset. This acquisition marks an important step for Petrolia Noco, adding significant production to our portfolio, allowing for growth and value creation through further exploration, field development and production deals”, said Morten Stenhaug, CEO of Petrolia Noco.<br> <br>Net average production (12.2575% WI) from the Brage field in Q3 2023 was 2.0 kboed. The remaining net reserves at year-end 2022 were 1.9 mmboe.<br><br>For further information, please contact:<br><br>Morten Stenhaug, CEO<br>+47 911 92 908<br><br>or<br><br>Erik von Krogh, CFO<br>+47 930 38 075</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Endring av aksje: Petrolia NOCO AS (PNO)</h2></td>
<td><h3>Corporate actions</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2023-11-28 13:23:45</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Det er foretatt endringer i Petrolia NOCO AS (ISIN:NO0010844301, ticker PNO).  Aksjebeholdningen er Ã¸ket fra 160 000 000 til 170 000 000. Emisjonsverdien er Ã¸ket fra 0 til 340 000 000.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
