<td><h2>PNO: Farm Down Agreements with Equinor Energy AS</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2022-02-24 14:11:01</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Petrolia NOCO AS is pleased to announce it has entered into two farm down agreements with Equinor Energy AS. <br><br>PL1013 and PL1013B<br>Petrolia NOCO will farm down a 40% participating interest of its 60% interest in its two exploration licenses PL1013 and PL1013B, where the exploration well Rafiki is planned to be drilled in 2023. As a part of the agreement Equinor Energy AS will assume operatorship of the licenses from Petrolia NOCO AS. <br><br>PL935<br>Petrolia NOCO will farm down a 10% participating interest of its 20% interest in PL935 where the exploration well Bounty is due to be drilled in the first half of 2022. <br><br>Both agreements are subject to license and regulatory approvals.<br><br>More information can be obtained from Robert Arnott, Executive Chairman of Petrolia NOCO AS. Telephone: +44-7775 818890, ra@petrolia.no</p></td>
</tr>
